    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p31-q55-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\cos 2\\theta=\\dfrac{1-\\tan^2\\theta}{1+\\tan^2\\theta}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1-\\tan^2\\theta}{1+\\tan^2\\theta}=\\cos 2\\theta$.\n\nMultiply numerator and denominator by $\\cos^2\\theta$, then use the cosine double-angle identity.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{RHS}&=\\frac{\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\\\text{RHS}&=\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta\\\\\\text{RHS}&=\\cos 2\\theta\\\\\\text{RHS}&=\\text{LHS}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q55-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find the exact value of $\\tan 15^\\circ$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2-\\sqrt3$.\n\nUse part a with $\\theta=15^\\circ$ and take the positive square root.",
          "worked": "Let $t=\\tan 15^\\circ$. From part a,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}&=\\frac{1-t^2}{1+t^2}\\\\\\sqrt3(1+t^2)&=2(1-t^2)\\\\(2+\\sqrt3)t^2&=2-\\sqrt3\\\\t^2&=\\frac{2-\\sqrt3}{2+\\sqrt3}\\\\t^2&=(2-\\sqrt3)^2.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $15^\\circ$ is in the first quadrant, $t>0$. Thus $\\tan 15^\\circ=2-\\sqrt3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      }
    ]
  },
